From 5a979e4c986ca3dfdfcba721bfa55a0976eda9a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 15:46:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(memory): enable Linux CXL/PMem/zswap/NVMe tiering when
 hardware exists

Consume the install-wizard memory_tiering flags. Discover CXL, DAX/PMem,
HBM NUMA, DAMON, weighted interleave, and spare NVMe; enable demotion and
NUMA balancing tiering mode for capacity policy; bind leftover Optane
App Direct via dax kmem; put zswap in front of a bounded swap file.
Future sysfs (CXL pooling, pghot, package-aware, guest CXL/NVDIMM) is
recorded as waiting_for_hardware until the kernel exposes it.

Live Processor & Memory now plots real meminfo, vmstat, PSI, zswap, swap,
and memory_tier nodelists instead of the demo catalog.
